# Git slash commands

When the user message contains these commands, execute immediately without asking for confirmation or Enter.

## `/commit`
- Commit only
- Do NOT push
- Follow the repo git safety protocol (status, diff, log, stage, commit, verify)
- Non-interactive only (no `-i`, no editors waiting for input)
- On Windows PowerShell, use a here-string for the commit message

## `/commitpush`
- Commit if there are changes
- Then push to the tracked remote (`git push -u origin HEAD` if upstream is missing)
- If no remote exists, create one with `gh repo create` only when clearly needed, then push
- Non-interactive only
- Return the commit hash and remote URL/status when done

## Shared behavior
- Never update git config
- Never force-push to main/master unless explicitly requested
- Never skip hooks unless explicitly requested
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens)
- If there is nothing to commit, say so; for `/commitpush`, still push if the branch is ahead
